{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973741-advice-me-for-my-second-chronicle-please-plot-inside","id":973741,"title":"Advice me for my second chronicle please (plot inside)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T03:22:55-07:00","id":973741,"title":"Advice me for my second chronicle please (plot inside)","content":"On Monday I ran the first session of my second chronicle of WtA. My group is made of 5 players and they are all cubs (so Garou without a Tribe) about to have their Rite of Passage. For this reason they were sent to investigate about one member of the sept that has disappeared during a big earthquake.<br /> <br /> This Garou (Grayleaf) is a Lupus and He usually acts like an &quot;ambassador&quot; with a nearby Sept composed by a large number of Red Talon. While they were going towards the site of the Earthquake they encountered the dead bodies of other members of that Sept (all Homid) killed by fireguns and silver bullets, and then they found a randezvous of two First team. Long story short: listening to the conversation between the two teams they figured out that they kidnapped Grayleaf and that they're taking him to &quot;The Pit&quot;.<br /> <br /> We interrupted the session just before the fight. Now: the plot here is that a popular company in the small town in which there was the earthquake has been secretly bought by the Pentex, with the plan of growing in the town to use it as a base to defeat (and corrupt) two Caerns nearby (one of these 2 is the one in which the players are). The Sept of the Red Talon discovered it and there solution was to ask for help to the spirit of Earthquake and destroy the town (you know, a typical Red Talon solution). The members of the other tribes in the sept were obviously against this solution so they met with Grayleaf, but they were killed by the First team that later kidnapped the Lupus so to lead the Sept of the players to think that his disappearance was Red Talon's fault.<br /> <br /> In addition the First teams were sent to recover the rests of a Wyrm Talon that they placed in the town so that the Red Talons were corrupted to the Wyrm while they were summoning Earthquake, so that the Sept of the Players think that there is no hand of the Wyrm in this.<br /> <br /> Now my question is: the players are probably gonna kill the two teams and discover the rests of the Talon (which, being a Talon, is not harmful to them). They will later have to discover the position of Grayleaf and return him to the Caern. Do you think this can be enough for a proper Rite of passage? They will have to gain the support of a totem spirit if they want to know where the lupus is, they will have to fight and they will have to think and discover more about this mysterious Pit that nobody in the area knows where it is).<br /> <br /> Would you add something else? I plan to let them finish this first &quot;chapter&quot; in one session or two, to continue then with the Sept officialy telling them to discover the exact location of this Pit.<br /> <br /> Do you have any additional advice? Do you see any weak point in my plot that I could enhance?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T01:44:45-07:00","id":978268,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong but this seems a bit heavy for a rite of passage... Unless they're all Fenrir. Are they all seeking entrance/ born of the same tribe? Is this a multi tribal rite? <br /> <br /> Let's be fair here, you can do it however you want. And honestly you'll likely enjoy the game more if you do it your way then getting muddled down by the rules heavy advice that can potentially come from this forum. <br /> <br /> For me a rite of passage would entail something particular for a certain tribe. This fetch quest though, as a prelim wouldn't be so bad. Once they have the info needed though I could see a Sept mobilizing major players, not necessarily new cubs (though they'd likely supplement numbers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:55:00-07:00","id":978516,"title":"","content":"Congrats on getting your claws wet, Panda!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973741-advice-me-for-my-second-chronicle-please-plot-inside?p=978268#post978268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong but this seems a bit heavy for a rite of passage... Unless they're all Fenrir.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. On the other hand, if the mission is 'find Greyleaf, the wayward lupus,' it may just be that the rite of passage spiraled out of control, and the sept leadership was simply unaware that Pentex and the Wyrm was behind the earthquake.<br /> <br /> If I were a member of the cub pack, I would probably report back to the home sept after the initial encounter with the Wyrm's forces. Things could escalate from there, but they would likely be successful in their rite, if they either rescue Greyleaf and/or kill a first team. A pack of cubs getting lucky enough to wipe two first teams without support might be pushing things.<br /> <br /> So after the initial scrap with Pentex's goons and potentially saving Greyleaf, the pack can pull back and regroup at the caern, sharing what they know. At this point, I would get other members of the sept involved, so there is comraderie and it doesn't seem like the other Garou are just sitting on their asses. Doesn't mean there has to be NPCs breathing down the pack's collective necks, just that they are part of a multi-pack search effort. If there was a Wyrmish stronghold in proximity to the caern, you bet the older Garou would do more than sic their wet-behind-the-ears pups on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be fair here, you can do it however you want. And honestly you'll likely enjoy the game more if you do it your way then getting muddled down by the rules heavy advice that can potentially come from this forum. </div> </div> </div>A-fucking-men brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 09-29-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:08:06-07:00","id":978523,"title":"","content":"Just posting to agree with the 2 posts above, especially the points <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3695_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3695\" data-vbnamecard=\"3695\">The Laughing Stranger</a> makes about getting the rest of the Sept involved once the scope of the issue is known.<br /> <br /> Sounds like fun though, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5825_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5825\" data-vbnamecard=\"5825\">Werepanda</a>, welcome to ST'ing Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:48:47-07:00","id":978683,"title":"","content":"I tend to use scouting missions as a Rite of Passage for groups. Garou are naturally violent, but they need to show that they can control their violence in order to be proper warriors of Gaia. I consider Garou to be the Space Marines of WoD, so I tend to give them missions that correspond to their Rank. Rank 1 are scouts, Rank 2 are warriors, Rank 3 are veterans, Rank 4 are officers, and Rank 5 are heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:53:37-07:00","id":978800,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree with the others this is a bit much for a Rite of Passage. My own chronicles vary but I tend to use the formation of the pack as the basis for my first chapter.<br /> <br /> Quests for the Elders to perform the Ritual to bond a Spirit to the pack have included:<br /> Recover the photos of a Garou caught on camera changing before the Vampire makes good his threat to release them to the public.<br /> Investigation of stolen wolves from a wolf sanctuary/rehabilitation center.<br /> Finding a missing kinfolk, I have used this several times if characters have kinfolk background.<br /> Investigate a horrific crime that may have been a first change situation if it was rescue the Garou from the mental facility holding him.<br /> <br /> The story as is does sound fun though and best of luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T02:51:37-07:00","id":978936,"title":"","content":"Echoing some of the above. Sounds awesome but with what they've achieved so far that should be Rite of Passage completed. Tackling two PX First Teams is a challenge for a pack of Cliath with a little experience and is risky for young Fostern even (First Teams being Pentex's anti Garou purposely trained and created force). <br /> <br /> Idea:: Possibly encourage them to flee the fight if they are set on going in hot. Hurt a couple of them bad as the two teams caught by surprise maybe lose a couple of members and then silver bullets and sickening Fomori powers retaliate. Cripple a 'packmate' (as they're not a true pack yet without a totem) with a volley of unsoakable Agg damage and make the rest of the pack have to carry his bloodied mangled body along. Don't kill them unless they do stupid stuff but just harrass them for a couple of turns until the flee to the Umbra (if there's a sensible place to do so) or have the Teams break off as there's other stuff to do. <br /> <br /> From that there's a bunch of game. Looking after the packmate as they flee. Making sure they're not leading anything back to the Caern (Litany you know). Getting to interact with the Wyrmfoe. Maybe discovering their Totem during the experience and maybe the Quest of the Pack (Prophecy of Phoenix stuff right there). Then when they've caught their breath it all slides nicely back into dealing with the very cool story you've started running them through <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:06:25-07:00","id":979026,"title":"","content":"Wow thanks I wasn't expecting answers anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it may just be that the rite of passage spiraled out of control, and the sept leadership was simply unaware that Pentex and the Wyrm was behind the earthquake. </div> </div> </div>That was exactly the point: the sept leadership was unaware of this Pentex plot, that's why they sent the cubs to find the missing Grayleaf.<br /> Anyway thank you for your advices, we played another session from my original post. Basically they killed the Fomori, recovered the rests of the Talon and learned that Greyleaf has been kidnapped and is being sent to the pit inside a truck. They talked between each other and then they decided to go on with their Rite and try to save Greyleaf asking for help to the realm of the spirits.<br /> <br /> Since being able to intercept the truck BEFORE it arrives to the Pit is a very difficult task (fortunately they decided they won't enter in the Pit in any case) , they asked Merlin to become their Totem. They pleged their service to Merlin and in return the spirit lead them through a secret passage in the Umbra so that they can get to the truck in time.<br /> <br /> We stopped the session when they came out of the Umbra while the truck is coming.<br /> <br /> My plan is to let them fight with a Cliath Spiral (a Ragabash sent to help the Fomori with Greyleaf and to bring him to the Pit) together with two or three weak Fomori to save Greyleaf.<br /> Do you think this is a feasible encounter for them? It's 5 garou vs 1 Spiral and 2/3 fomori with just a silver bullet each. I think they could handle it, but maybe I am wrong.<br /> <br /> Again, thanks for your comment they were very precious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> As others on this thread suggested after this Rite of Passage as a pack, I'd like them to have a very small individual test to see if they're accepted by the spirit of the Tribes they chose. Could you help me in finding something taht suits the tribe and the auspice?<br /> <br /> These are their auspices with their (maybe) future tribe.<br /> <br /> - Galliard wannabe Glass Walker: really no idea, maybe I should read the GW tribebook for hints, but what could Cockroach expect from a Galliard of his Tribe? <br /> <br /> - Ahroun wannabe Silverfang/Fenrir: this character has Pure Breed 5 and He descend from Charles I of Anjou (which was a Garou Silverfang in my campaign). He's stuck between following his ancestors joining Falcon's children or joining the Get of Fenris (his &quot;philosophy&quot; of life is very close to the Get). In the first case I thought about a meeting with the eldest Silver Fang in the sept to test his leadership, while in the second case maybe a fight would be better.<br /> <br /> - Theurge wannabe Children of Gaia: the Sept Leader is a Children of Gaia and I'd like to do something concerning the spirit world but really I don't know. Maybe the sept leader could try to summon a spirit close to unicorn to see how she interact with him to find some informations?<br /> <br /> - Ragabash wannabe Shadowlord: no ideas<br /> <br /> - Philodox wannabe Stargazer: there's no Stargazer in the Sept, but he has Ancestors so he's aware of his history and of his tribe. Some test may include proving the capacity to resist Frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","user":"Werepanda","date":". 09-30-2016, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:37:39-07:00","id":979148,"title":"","content":"Sounds good! I like that you made it hard to stop the truck, but not impossible, and when the pups took the steps to catch it with the help of a spirit patron, you let it happen.<br /> <br /> As for exact encounter strength, what you haves sounds fine- I did a very similar first fight for my pack- a single Black Spiral Dancer had kidnapped some kids and was binding banes into them when the pack arrived, so they had to fight/restrain the weak little mockeries and kill the Dancer himself. Figuring out what your pack can and can't handle is kind of tricky, but you will get a feel for it. That being said, silver is scary, but if the Garou hit hard and smart most of the Wyrm mutants will probably die before they get their shots off.<br /> <br /> I will say that silver has a strong element of unpredictability- if you roll well you might just have a dead player on your hands.<br /> <br /> As for your edit,<br /> <br /> Cockroach wants information. Galliards help preserve that information, and share it when it would be useful. Perhaps Cockroach wants some tidbit of lore to be rediscovered and then made known- something that might provide a plot hook later down the road?<br /> <br /> The Ahroun is probably going to get some serious pushback from the Silver Fangs- squandering Falcon's noble blood should be no light matter. I would probably have the Elders council him to seek out both totems, and then each would present a combat challenge that he could overcome, something emblematic. At the risk of being a bit stereotypical, perhaps present the Silver Fang challenge as one befitting a warlord, a driven warrior who inspires and perhaps frightens his lessers (hell, maybe even have an ancestor-fueled flashback to Charles' life and have the Ahroun fight in Charles' place, either in the Crusades or against the Hohenstaufen). On the other hand, the Fenris-wolf would present the opportunity to be an embodiment of the totem's rage and fury, overcoming pain through strength and tenacity. I still like the historical angle here, maybe fight a wicked, bloodthirsty Aenir in the frozen wastes, the driving snow and sub-zero winds biting nearly as hard as the crazed false god.<br /> <br /> I think Unicorn would want something pure protected or healed. After Pentex's assault, I am sure there are Naturae spirits in need of help (there was an earthquake, maybe it hurt or frightened some elementals nearby).<br /> <br /> Ragabash Shadow Lord? Have a stormcrow meet with the pup and charge them to find a weakness in a rival (or packmate!) and... wait. Save it for use later.<br /> <br /> Stargazers serve Chimera, so a dream quest that involves justice-oriented riddles or making judgement calls with strange repercussions may be in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:21:55-07:00","id":979852,"title":"","content":"Hm, Stargazers are a problem actually, as they have left the Garou Nation for the Beast Courts. While there are exceptions, the tribe is not accepting members from the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:43:59-07:00","id":979931,"title":"","content":"Stargazer shoud be fine as is Totem acceptance that they'd be after, the Garou Nation thing was...weird and mostly glossed over as there were plenty of the Tribe active outside the beast courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T10:56:29-07:00","id":980888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/973741-advice-me-for-my-second-chronicle-please-plot-inside?p=979148#post979148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds good! I like that you made it hard to stop the truck, but not impossible, and when the pups took the steps to catch it with the help of a spirit patron, you let it happen.<br /> <br /> As for exact encounter strength, what you haves sounds fine- I did a very similar first fight for my pack- a single Black Spiral Dancer had kidnapped some kids and was binding banes into them when the pack arrived, so they had to fight/restrain the weak little mockeries and kill the Dancer himself. Figuring out what your pack can and can't handle is kind of tricky, but you will get a feel for it. That being said, silver is scary, but if the Garou hit hard and smart most of the Wyrm mutants will probably die before they get their shots off.<br /> <br /> I will say that silver has a strong element of unpredictability- if you roll well you might just have a dead player on your hands.<br /> <br /> As for your edit,<br /> <br /> Cockroach wants information. Galliards help preserve that information, and share it when it would be useful. Perhaps Cockroach wants some tidbit of lore to be rediscovered and then made known- something that might provide a plot hook later down the road?<br /> <br /> The Ahroun is probably going to get some serious pushback from the Silver Fangs- squandering Falcon's noble blood should be no light matter. I would probably have the Elders council him to seek out both totems, and then each would present a combat challenge that he could overcome, something emblematic. At the risk of being a bit stereotypical, perhaps present the Silver Fang challenge as one befitting a warlord, a driven warrior who inspires and perhaps frightens his lessers (hell, maybe even have an ancestor-fueled flashback to Charles' life and have the Ahroun fight in Charles' place, either in the Crusades or against the Hohenstaufen). On the other hand, the Fenris-wolf would present the opportunity to be an embodiment of the totem's rage and fury, overcoming pain through strength and tenacity. I still like the historical angle here, maybe fight a wicked, bloodthirsty Aenir in the frozen wastes, the driving snow and sub-zero winds biting nearly as hard as the crazed false god.<br /> <br /> I think Unicorn would want something pure protected or healed. After Pentex's assault, I am sure there are Naturae spirits in need of help (there was an earthquake, maybe it hurt or frightened some elementals nearby).<br /> <br /> Ragabash Shadow Lord? Have a stormcrow meet with the pup and charge them to find a weakness in a rival (or packmate!) and... wait. Save it for use later.<br /> <br /> Stargazers serve Chimera, so a dream quest that involves justice-oriented riddles or making judgement calls with strange repercussions may be in order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, you really inspired me. Tomorrow we are going to have our gaming session, I'll let you know what happens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hm, Stargazers are a problem actually, as they have left the Garou Nation for the Beast Courts. While there are exceptions, the tribe is not accepting members from the Garou Nation. </div> </div> </div>We play in the W20 where, as I understand, this is not a huge problem as it was in Rev.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}